WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.840
After all this time, Spider-Man never met&nbsp;
Hawkeye? Or Loki? What kind of spider is he,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.760
anyway? A recluse? Want more surprising MCU heroes&nbsp;
that never entered Spidey's web? Keep watching.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.240
While it's true that Peter Parker and&nbsp;
Natasha Romanoff fought as allies under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.240
team Tony Stark in "Captain America:&nbsp;
Civil War," the two arachnid-themed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.280
Avengers didn't really get to know&nbsp;
each other at the Airport battle.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.520
As audiences saw in Peter's videos of his&nbsp;
trip to Germany in "Spider-Man: Homecoming,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.240
the young hero didn't take part in Iron Man's&nbsp;
strategic meetings with his fellow Sokovia Accords&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.200
enforcers — and when Spider-Man leapt into battle,&nbsp;
most of his energy and attention went to fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.840
the Falcon, the Winter Soldier, Captain America,&nbsp;
and Ant-Man. By the time the skirmish ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.080
Natasha had already run away after turning&nbsp;
traitor, while Spider-Man was taken out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.040
commission due to injuries sustained from the&nbsp;
giant-sized Ant-Man's accidental backhand.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.280
Spider-Man and the Black Widow would later&nbsp;
find themselves fighting against a common enemy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.920
once more, albeit on different battlegrounds,&nbsp;
in "Avengers: Infinity War," but it doesn't seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.960
like they had a chance to cross paths. Spidey was&nbsp;
taking the fight directly to Thanos on Titan while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.040
Black Widow fought in the Battle of Wakanda&nbsp;
to stop Thanos' forces from taking the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.160
Infinity Stone. Sadly, Peter was among those who&nbsp;
vanished in the Blip — and while he did manage to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.480
return to the land of the living, Natasha had&nbsp;
to sacrifice her life to make that possible.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.200
Save for his impromptu trip to space in "Avengers:&nbsp;
Infinity War," the MCU's Spider-Man is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.240
self-described "friendly neighborhood" hero who's&nbsp;
more comfortable going on grounded, street-level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.040
adventures. Unsurprisingly, many of the heroes&nbsp;
he hasn't met in this universe are of the cosmic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.920
variety — and you can't get more otherworldly&nbsp;
than the God of Thunder himself, Thor.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.160
The first time Spider-Man and Thor had an&nbsp;
opportunity to meet each other was during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.960
the final battle in "Avengers: Endgame." However,&nbsp;
they didn't even get the chance to banter — though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.520
the webslinger did get to fly through the sky&nbsp;
via Mjolnir, thanks to a last-minute save from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.560
the unexpectedly worthy Steve Rogers. After&nbsp;
Tony Stark's funeral, the Asgardian decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.120
to join the Guardians of the Galaxy as part&nbsp;
of a period of self-reflection, while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.240
spider-powered teenager continued to serve as one&nbsp;
of New York's few remaining active superheroes.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.680
In the comics, Peter Parker and Bruce Banner&nbsp;
are among the brightest scientific minds in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.200
their universe. As for their alter-egos, while&nbsp;
the Hulk is one of Earth's mightiest warriors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.560
Spider-Man's no slouch in the&nbsp;
strength department, either. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.160
it would have been simultaneously amazing and&nbsp;
incredible to see Peter Parker talk science&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:33.600
with Bruce Banner — and to watch Spider-Man&nbsp;
and the Hulk have a Marvel-ous team-up.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.600
While Spider-Man was busy helping Tony Stark&nbsp;
bring in Steve Rogers in "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.160
Civil War," the green behemoth was off-world.&nbsp;
In "Avengers: Infinity War," Spider-Man lent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.080
a much-needed helping hand to Iron Man in&nbsp;
fighting off Cull Obsidian, largely because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.080
the Hulk didn't want to come out of Bruce&nbsp;
following his defeat at the hands of Thanos.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.720
It doesn't seem like Spidey and Bruce had much of&nbsp;
a chance to trade contact info during the battle.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.960
While Webhead and Jade Jaws both pitched&nbsp;
in during the final battle in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.840
Endgame," the two could-have-been-Science-Bros&nbsp;
didn't really get the chance to partner up.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.080
All things considered, the Guardians of&nbsp;
the Galaxy would probably seem like an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.320
interesting crew for Peter Parker: a weirdly&nbsp;
charismatic team of oddballs and outlaws with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.800
a strange sense of humor. While he did get&nbsp;
to converse with half the team in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.760
Infinity War," the fact that Peter hadn't had&nbsp;
any meaningful interactions with Rocket, Groot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.280
or Gamora should be rectified&nbsp;
in a future MCU production.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.280
As for the other half of the team, Spider-Man&nbsp;
fought alongside Star-Lord, Drax, Mantis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.360
and Nebula on Titan, in a failed attempt&nbsp;
to take the Infinity Gauntlet from Thanos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.160
before he could complete the Infinity Stones.&nbsp;
This ended in Spidey and some of the surviving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.800
Guardians getting dusted and staying dead for&nbsp;
five years. Upon their return in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.480
Endgame," Spider-Man found himself allied&nbsp;
in battle with the Guardians once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.520
as well as a time-displaced version of Gamora.&nbsp;
However, despite being on the same battlefield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.480
Spider-Man didn't really get the&nbsp;
opportunity to meet the rest of the crew.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.880
When Ant-Man sided with Captain America's team in&nbsp;
"Captain America: Civil War," he didn't have Wasp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.240
on his side. For a brief period of time, though,&nbsp;
the Wasp almost made it to Team Cap's roster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.000
before the Russo brothers decided that the&nbsp;
story of her introduction would be better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.240
served in a movie that didn't already have too&nbsp;
many characters and storylines on its plate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.080
While the decision to have Scott Lang&nbsp;
join Team Cap without Hope van Dyne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.480
ultimately allowed her to have a proper official&nbsp;
costumed debut in "Ant-Man and the Wasp,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.280
it was still a missed opportunity for the stinging&nbsp;
superheroine to butt heads against Spider-Man.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.680
Spider-Man and the Wasp would later get a shot&nbsp;
at fighting on the same side in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.120
Endgame," following their revival after&nbsp;
getting dusted by Thanos. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.680
they still didn't get the chance to interact&nbsp;
with each other during the extremely crowded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.080
final fight — and despite the fact that&nbsp;
they both showed up at Tony Stark's funeral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.360
audiences didn't get to see them&nbsp;
meet each other or swap stories.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:54.000
Despite her significant role in Thor's early MCU&nbsp;
mythology, Lady Sif hasn't been seen that often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.880
in subsequent movies. In fact, she didn't even&nbsp;
show up in "Thor: Ragnarok," and was confirmed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.440
have died during the Blip in "Avengers: Infinity&nbsp;
War." It's safe to assume that like the rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.240
the heroes brought back in "Avengers: Endgame,"&nbsp;
the fierce Asgardian warrior was alive during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.600
final battle against Thanos, but audiences didn't&nbsp;
get to see her if so. Incidentally, this also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.080
meant that Spider-Man likely never got to meet&nbsp;
her or witness her abilities on the battlefield.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.120
Realistically, there probably isn't much that&nbsp;
Spider-Man and Lady Sif would have to talk about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.440
nor would they really have any solid reason to&nbsp;
interact. Nevertheless, it's always a treat to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.080
see how a conversation between an Earthling&nbsp;
and an Asgardian goes — especially if said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:38.080
conversation involved the jocular Spider-Man&nbsp;
and the somewhat serious Lady Sif. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.720
hopefully they get along&nbsp;
better than Sif and Loki did.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.400
"I hope you know you deserve to&nbsp;
be alone and you always will be.”

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:52.720
Speaking of the God of Mischief, if&nbsp;
Peter Parker ever gets to meet Loki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.960
their encounter would doubtlessly&nbsp;
be full of hilarity. Spider-Man's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.320
humorous jabs and naive observations would&nbsp;
probably amuse, or irk, the trickster god,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.920
while Loki's penchant for deception and&nbsp;
dishonesty would likely befuddle the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.960
webslinger. That's why it's a shame these two&nbsp;
characters have never met in an MCU production.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:14.080
Despite the fact that Loki has&nbsp;
been on Earth multiple times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.640
none of his Midgardian adventures have caused&nbsp;
his path to cross with Spider-Man. While Spidey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.680
and the rest of the Avengers were busy&nbsp;
trying to fend off Thanos in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.160
Endgame," a version of Loki that branched out&nbsp;
from the timeline of 2012's "The Avengers"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.840
ended up having his own adventures&nbsp;
in his eponymous Disney+ show.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.640
If one were to be technical about it, Peter&nbsp;
Parker did have at least one significant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.200
albeit brief, moment of collaboration with King&nbsp;
T'Challa: At a critical point in "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:45.760
Endgame," the teen superhero snags the Infinity&nbsp;
Gauntlet from Black Panther with a webline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.160
in an attempt to take it as far away from Thanos&nbsp;
as possible. Despite this, however, the Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.400
Panther still belongs on this list, simply&nbsp;
because he and Spider-Man have not really had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.240
any meaningful and direct interactions, despite&nbsp;
being on the same battlefield not once, but twice.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.520
The first opportunity that Spider-Man&nbsp;
and the Black Panther could have had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.720
for formal introductions took place&nbsp;
in "Captain America: Civil War,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.200
during the lengthy airport battle scene. However,&nbsp;
both superheroes had their hands full trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.960
subdue their respective opponents and didn't&nbsp;
really get the opportunity for chit-chat.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.120
Considering that Chadwick Boseman sadly&nbsp;
passed away in 2020, it seems that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:24.240
brief interaction in "Endgame" will be the extent&nbsp;
of their relationship for the foreseeable future.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:30.000
Clint Barton is one of the MCU's founding&nbsp;
Avengers, and also happens to be one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.040
most oft-underestimated heroes in the cinematic&nbsp;
universe due to his lack of fancy abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.440
Nevertheless, he has proven countless times that&nbsp;
he can hold his own in the company of Earth's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:44.960
mightiest heroes, and has played a crucial role&nbsp;
in virtually every major battle since the Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.240
were founded. He even helped the heroes win the&nbsp;
day against Thanos' forces in "Avengers: Endgame."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:55.520
Unfortunately, his part in that grand skirmish&nbsp;
did not involve meeting Spider-Man at all.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:01.600
Among all the MCU's superpowered heroes, Peter&nbsp;
Parker is perhaps the most human. Without a doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:05.840
he would find some form of kinship in Clint,&nbsp;
who could probably teach him a thing or two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.640
about acting more mature and getting over his&nbsp;
insecurities in front of the costumed superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.280
crowd. If Hawkeye's uneasy partnership with&nbsp;
Kate Bishop in the Disney+ "Hawkeye" series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.360
is any indication, the Avenging Archer&nbsp;
would actually make a better teacher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.240
for a young hero like Spider-Man&nbsp;
than he'd be willing to admit.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.000
Spider-Man and the Vision fought side by side in&nbsp;
"Captain America: Civil War" under the leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.320
of Iron Man. However, much like the other&nbsp;
heroes that joined Team Tony, Spider-Man didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.640
get the chance to interact with the Infinity&nbsp;
Stone-powered synthezoid on the silver screen.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:41.120
This lack of interaction between Spider-Man&nbsp;
and the Vision in MCU movies is a missed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.200
opportunity for the young scientist to be&nbsp;
able to understand cutting-edge technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:49.680
and artificial intelligence from a radically&nbsp;
different point of view. In a world full of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:55.040
gamma-powered monster men and hammer-wielding&nbsp;
gods, an artificial being like the Vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.280
still pushes the boundaries of modern&nbsp;
technology — and there's little doubt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:04.960
the science-inclined Spider-Man would be thrilled&nbsp;
at the prospect of talking to a lifelike machine.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.160
On the flipside, spending more time&nbsp;
with Spider-Man could help the Vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:11.680
to better understand what it means to&nbsp;
be a human being. Hopefully, a future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:16.240
Marvel movie could provide an opportunity&nbsp;
for Peter to flex his scientific prowess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.160
while helping the Vision in his mission&nbsp;
to come to terms with his own humanity.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.280
For the first decade of the MCU's run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.400
Shang-Chi has been completely absent from silver&nbsp;
screen depictions of its world-shaking events.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.600
And because the superheroic martial artist only&nbsp;
made his debut in 2021's "Shang-Chi," it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.240
surprising that he hasn't had the chance to meet&nbsp;
many of the MCU's heroes, including Spider-Man.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.040
That said, it's worth noting&nbsp;
that "Shang-Chi" takes place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.600
after the Blip was undone and likely before&nbsp;
the events of "Spider-Man: Far From Home."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.960
In other words, when Shang-Chi&nbsp;
first shows up on everyone's radar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:53.920
Peter Parker isn't on the run yet as a result of&nbsp;
Mysterio blowing his secret identity wide open.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.160
Realistically, there's plenty of time&nbsp;
for Spider-Man and Shang-Chi to meet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.600
Maybe Shang-Chi could teach Peter Parker a&nbsp;
thing or two when it comes to martial arts.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.720
"You have the wrong guy! Does&nbsp;
he look like he can fight?"

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:17.600
Despite being on Earth for an extremely long time,&nbsp;
the Eternals have been conspicuously absent from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.560
virtually all of the major battles that kept it&nbsp;
safe from alien invaders and would-be conquerors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:27.600
This explains why the MCU heroes, including&nbsp;
Spider-Man, have never crossed paths with them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.000
in previous films. However, with the departure&nbsp;
of many MCU mainstays following the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.840
of "Avengers: Endgame," there's plenty&nbsp;
of room in the sandbox for the Eternals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:40.240
to play — and just as many opportunities for&nbsp;
them to get tangled up in Spider-Man's web.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.880
In an interview with Screen Rant, the cast&nbsp;
members were asked which MCU heroes they'd be most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:49.920
excited to work with. Interestingly, two of them&nbsp;
name-dropped Spider-Man. According to Don Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.040
he'd love to test his strength against the Hulk&nbsp;
or team up with Spider-Man if he reprises his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.040 --> 00:11:00.080
role as Gilgamesh. Meanwhile, for Lia McHugh,&nbsp;
who plays Sprite, the answer is a no-brainer:

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:05.760
"[O]f course, Spider-Man. Tom Holland, duh. I&nbsp;
would absolutely love to be in a movie with him."

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.360
Hey, get in line!

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.400
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:13.200
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite movies are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:24.320
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

